WEBVTT

00:05:59.577 --> 00:06:02.266
Try to come back from that
when you're campaigning.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:06.201
Martine Haas: I think in some ways,
we are adapting very, very fast right now.

00:06:06.225 --> 00:06:09.376
We are the experiment that
will create the data. (Laughs)

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.527
AG: Martine Haas is
my colleague at Wharton

00:06:11.551 --> 00:06:14.976
and a renowned expert
on how teams collaborate at a distance.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.856
Now she isn't just studying it.
She's living it.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.941
MH: I've been working
to kind of get my setup really functional,

00:06:20.965 --> 00:06:24.266
and I invested in a screen
to separate my workspace

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.148
from the rest of the room that I'm in.

00:06:26.172 --> 00:06:29.176
I open the screen ceremoniously
in the morning,

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.820
and then I close it ceremoniously.